  New Seminar Series
     Beginning this summer, DSW Group, Softbite International, and
  Zachary Software will each reach, collectively, more than 50
  cities worldwide to offer developers training on using Delphi to
  build stand-alone, LAN and Client/Server applications.  Each
  company will provide one- and two-day international seminars
  beginning in July and running throughout the year.
     "Delphi has taken the development community by storm," said
  Kevin Smith, a partner with Softbite International.  "We see our
  Delphi World Tour as a great opportunity to help thousands of
  developers around the world become Delphi experts."
     "Our Information Services Department has sent at least 50
  employees to the Delphi Seminars, and some of those developers
  were able to create an application within just a few days after
  the seminar," said Nam Huynh, senior programmer for the City of
  Los Angeles.  "We have seen immediate results from these
  trainings and highly recommend them to other Delphi developers."
     For information on seminar locations and dates, as well as
  Borland regional training seminars, developers may log on to
  Borland's Internet World Wide Web site at HTPP://www.borland.com.
  Developers may also contact the following seminar companies
  directly for schedules and registration forms at these numbers:

